    "updated_at": "2018-09-20T14:02:15Z",
    "body": "Adding back the hierachy restrictions for this event targetting is unforunate. We are forcing users into a model of how to design their application that the content must be present in the child of the current fullscreen element.Think of a series of divs that are all siblings and you click 'next'. Which would change the fullscreen element to the next element. In order to replicate that you'd need to do a bunch of tree modifications. Also it prevents you from re-entering a fullscreen element already on the stack. \r\n\r\n@domenic  Adding Domenic in case he has any ideas here.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
