    "created_at": "2018-10-19T23:54:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-10-19T23:54:26Z",
    "body": "> Think of a series of divs that are all siblings and you click 'next'. Which would change the fullscreen element to the next element.\r\n\r\nThat is not a usecase that the current Fullscreen API is supposed to support. You would end up having lots of elements in the fullscreen layer, and you cannot exit fullscreen in one statement (unless we add #70).\r\n\r\nIf we want to serve this usecase, we may want an API like `requestFullscreen({ replace: true })` or so, rather than supporting multi-leaf.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
